{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>There shall be no kedeshah.</b> One set apart and designated for prostitution." "<b>And there shall be no kadesh.</b> Designated for male intercourse; and Onkelos rendered: ״לָא תְהֵא אִתְּתָא מִבְּנָת יִשְׂרָאֵל לִגְבַר עָבֵד״ — for she too is set apart for an act of prostitution, since kiddushin do not take hold for him with her, for they were likened to a donkey, as it says: ״Stay here with the donkey״ (שְׁבוּ לָכֶם פֹּה עִם הַחֲמוֹר) — with one likened to a donkey; and ״לָא יִסַּב גַּבְרָא מִבְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אִתְּתָא אָמָה״ — for he too becomes a kadesh through her, for all his acts of intercourse are acts of prostitution, since kiddushin do not take hold for him with her (see Kiddushin 68)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:09.901226853Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}